# [Kth Smallest Element in a BST](https://leetcode.com/problems/kth-smallest-element-in-a-bst/)

## Approach: Inorder Traversal (DFS)

1. Perform an inorder traversal of the BST (Left → Root → Right).
2. Inorder traversal visits BST nodes in ascending order.
3. Decrement `k` whenever a node is visited.
4. When `k` becomes zero, the current node contains the kth smallest element.
5. Store its value in `ans` and return it.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    void solve(TreeNode* root,int&k,int&ans){
        if(!root)return;

        solve(root->left,k,ans);

        if(root)k--;

        if(k == 0){
            ans = root->val;
            return;
        }

        solve(root->right,k,ans);
    }

    int kthSmallest(TreeNode* root, int k) {
        int ans = -1;
        solve(root,k,ans);
        return ans;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(N)\) — In the worst case, all nodes may be visited.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(H)\) — Recursion stack, where \(H\) is the height of the tree.
